---
name: is_user_logged_in
redirect_to: '{% if context.current_user %}/401{% else %}/sign-in{% endif %}'
metadata: {
    "auth_policy_name": "User Authentication"
}
---

{% liquid
  graphql data = 'account/get_current_user'

  assign user_profile = data.current_user.client | first

  comment
    Policy requires an attached client profile. Explicitly echo true/false
    to avoid implicit behavior that could lead to unexpected access.

    A signed-out visitor is sent to /sign-in. A signed-in user with no client
    profile (for example a contact created by the CRM) is not sent to sign in,
    because the sign-in page would send them straight back. This policy's
    redirect names /401, but such a user also fails is_user_allowed, and when
    several policies fail the one created first decides the redirect. That is
    is_user_allowed, so in practice they go to /verify-2fa and end on /403.
    The platform adds
    return_to=<the page asked for> to the redirect; the sign-in page passes it
    through account/safe_return_to.
  endcomment
  if user_profile != blank
    echo true
  else
    echo false
  endif
%}